#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:952
msgid "am and apply:"
msgstr "am と apply について:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:958
msgid ""
"apply, without `--index` or `--cached`, relies on files being present in the "
"working copy, and also writes to them unconditionally.  As such, it should "
"first check for the files' presence, and if found to be SKIP_WORKTREE, then "
"clear the bit and vivify the paths, then do its work.  Currently, it just "
"throws an error."
msgstr ""
"apply は、 `--index` または `--cached` を指定しないと、 作業コピーに存在する"
"ファイルに依存し、 また、 それらに無条件に書き込みます。 そのため、 最初に"
"ファイルの存在を確認し、 SKIP_WORKTREE であることが判明した場合は、 ビットを"
"クリアしてパスを復活(vivify)させてから作業を実行する必要があります。 現時点で"
"は、 エラーが投げられるだけです。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:963
msgid ""
"apply, with either `--cached` or `--index`, will not preserve the "
"SKIP_WORKTREE bit.  This is fine if the file has conflicts, but otherwise "
"SKIP_WORKTREE bits should be preserved for --cached and probably also for --"
"index."
msgstr ""
"`--cached` または `--index` を指定して apply を実行すると、 SKIP_WORKTREE "
"ビットは保持されません。 ファイルに競合がある場合はこれで問題ありませんが、 "
"そうでない場合は、 SKIP_WORKTREE ビットを `--cached` と、 おそらく `--index` "
"に対しても保存するべきです。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:970
msgid ""
"am, if there are no conflicts, will vivify files and fail to preserve the "
"SKIP_WORKTREE bit.  If there are conflicts and `-3` is not specified, it "
"will vivify files and then complain the patch doesn't apply.  If there are "
"conflicts and `-3` is specified, it will vivify files and then complain that "
"those vivified files would be overwritten by merge."
msgstr ""
"am は、 競合がない場合、 ファイルを復活(vivify)させ、 SKIP_WORKTREE ビットの"
"保存に失敗します。 競合があり、 `-3` が指定されていない場合、 ファイルは復活"
"(vivify)後、 パッチが適用されないというメッセージが表示されます。 競合があ"
"り、 `-3` が指定されている場合、 ファイルを復活(vivify)させ、 それらの復活"
"(vivify)したファイルがマージによって上書きされると警告します。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:972
msgid "reset --hard:"
msgstr "`reset --hard` について:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:975
msgid ""
"reset --hard provides confusing error message (works correctly, but misleads "
"the user into believing it didn't):"
msgstr ""
"`reset --hard` は、 以下のような混乱を招くエラー・メッセージを表示します(それ"
"は正しく動作しますが、ユーザーに動作しなかったと誤解させます):"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:991
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ touch addme\n"
"$ git add addme\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H addme\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git reset --hard                           # usually works great\n"
"error: Path 'addme' not uptodate; will not remove from working tree.\n"
"HEAD is now at bdbbb6f third\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ ls -1\n"
"tracked\n"
msgstr ""
"$ touch addme\n"
"$ git add addme\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H addme\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git reset --hard                           # usually works great\n"
"error: Path 'addme' not uptodate; will not remove from working tree.\n"
"HEAD is now at bdbbb6f third\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ ls -1\n"
"tracked\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:995
msgid ""
"`git reset --hard` DID remove addme from the index and the working tree, "
"contrary to the error message, but in line with how reset --hard should "
"behave."
msgstr ""
"`git replace --hard` は、 エラー・メッセージとは裏腹に、 インデックスと作業ツ"
"リーから addme を削除しましたが、 それは `reset --hard` の振る舞いに沿って行"
"われたものです。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1001
msgid ""
"`read-tree` doesn't apply the 'SKIP_WORKTREE' bit to *any* of the entries it "
"reads into the index, resulting in all your files suddenly appearing to be "
"\"deleted\"."
msgstr ""
"`read-tree` は、 インデックスに読み込む 「どのエントリ」にも `SKIP_WORKTREE` "
"ビットを適用しないため、 すべてのファイルが突然「削除」されたように見えます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1003
msgid "Checkout, restore:"
msgstr "Checkout、 restore について:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1005
msgid "These command do not handle path & revision arguments appropriately:"
msgstr "以下のコマンドは、 パスとリビジョンの引数を適切に処理しません:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1031
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ ls\n"
"tracked\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$ git checkout -- '*skipped'\n"
"error: pathspec '*skipped' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git ls-files -- '*skipped'\n"
"tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD -- '*skipped'\n"
"error: pathspec '*skipped' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git ls-tree HEAD | grep skipped\n"
"100644 blob 276f5a64354b791b13840f02047738c77ad0584f\ttracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD~1 -- '*skipped'\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"H tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"M  tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD -- '*skipped'\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$ ls\n"
"tracked\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$ git checkout -- '*skipped'\n"
"error: pathspec '*skipped' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git ls-files -- '*skipped'\n"
"tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD -- '*skipped'\n"
"error: pathspec '*skipped' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git ls-tree HEAD | grep skipped\n"
"100644 blob 276f5a64354b791b13840f02047738c77ad0584f\ttracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD~1 -- '*skipped'\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"H tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"M  tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD -- '*skipped'\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1036
msgid ""
"Note that checkout without a revision (or restore --staged) fails to find a "
"file to restore from the index, even though ls-files shows such a file "
"certainly exists."
msgstr ""
"注意: リビジョンなしの checkout (または `restore --staged`)では、 ls-files で"
"そのようなファイルが確かに存在することが示されている場合でも、 インデックスか"
"ら復元(restore)するファイルが見つからないことに注意してください。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1040
msgid ""
"Similar issues occur with HEAD (--source=HEAD in restore's case), but "
"suddenly works when HEAD~1 is specified.  And then after that it will work "
"with HEAD specified, even though it didn't before."
msgstr ""
"同様の問題が HEAD (restore の場合は `--source=HEAD`)でも発生しますが、 "
"HEAD~1 が指定されると突然機能するようになります。 その後、 以前は機能しなかっ"
"たとしても、 HEAD を指定しても機能するようになります。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1042
msgid "Directories are also an issue:"
msgstr "ディレクトリにも問題があります:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1048
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git sparse-checkout set nomatches\n"
"$ git status\n"
"On branch main\n"
"You are in a sparse checkout with 0% of tracked files present.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ git sparse-checkout set nomatches\n"
"$ git status\n"
"On branch main\n"
"You are in a sparse checkout with 0% of tracked files present.\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1057
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"nothing to commit, working tree clean\n"
"$ git checkout .\n"
"error: pathspec '.' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD~1 .\n"
"Updated 1 path from 58916d9\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"S tracked\n"
"H tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
msgstr ""
"nothing to commit, working tree clean\n"
"$ git checkout .\n"
"error: pathspec '.' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD~1 .\n"
"Updated 1 path from 58916d9\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"S tracked\n"
"H tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1060
msgid "checkout and restore --staged, continued:"
msgstr "checkout と `restore --staged` の続き:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1064
msgid ""
"These commands do not correctly scope operations to the sparse "
"specification, and make it worse by not setting important SKIP_WORKTREE bits:"
msgstr ""
"以下のコマンドは、 操作のスコープをスパース仕様に対して正しく設定しておら"
"ず、 重要な SKIP_WORKTREE ビットを設定しないため、 事態はさらに悪化します:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1071
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git restore --source OLDREV --staged outside-sparse-cone/\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"MD outside-sparse-cone/file1\n"
"MD outside-sparse-cone/file2\n"
"MD outside-sparse-cone/file3\n"
msgstr ""
"$ git restore --source OLDREV --staged outside-sparse-cone/\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"MD outside-sparse-cone/file1\n"
"MD outside-sparse-cone/file2\n"
"MD outside-sparse-cone/file3\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1076
msgid ""
"We can add a --scope=all mode to `git restore` to let it operate outside the "
"sparse specification, but then it will be important to set the SKIP_WORKTREE "
